node_modules/
.env

# src/data/teamCache/ is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# It was, and that made the Arena unusable once deployed. The cache is what
# spares the server a full franchise walk -- 60-160 sequential NBA calls -- and
# with the directory ignored, the deployed instance shipped with none of it. A
# measured cold request for one team's history took 37 MINUTES and never
# returned, which is what "82-0 is slow and doesn't work" actually was.
#
# Render's disk is ephemeral too, so anything fetched in production is lost on
# every restart and re-walked from scratch. Committing the caches is what makes
# them a shipped artifact rather than a local convenience -- the same approach
# services/api/data_cache/ already takes, at a similar size.
#
# Refresh them with the server running: the startup pass repairs gaps by itself
# (see teamPlayersCache.js), then commit whatever changed.
